---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BookingCTA from '../components/BookingCTA.astro';
import { images, site, yearsActive, influences, genres, contact, venueCount } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`Gagandip Singh — DJ Gags. ${yearsActive} years behind the decks, from a first show in 2000 to six residencies, Goa main stages and the country's biggest campus circuit.`}
>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Story</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-3xl font-display text-[clamp(2.5rem,8vw,5.5rem)] leading-[0.92] text-bone">
        Calm off stage. A hive mind on it.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-line py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-5 sm:px-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,3fr)] md:gap-16">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="border border-line">
          <img
            src={images.portrait}
            alt="Studio portrait of DJ Gags"
            class="w-full object-cover"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="border border-line bg-surface p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">At a Glance</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-muted">Name</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-bone">{site.legalName}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-muted">Base</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-bone">{site.city}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-muted">Active since</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-bone">{site.careerStart}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-muted">Sound</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-bone">{genres.join(' · ')}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-muted">Studio</dt>
              <dd class="text-right text-bone">{contact.label}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[15px] leading-[1.85] text-body">
        <p class="font-serif text-xl italic leading-relaxed text-bone sm:text-2xl">
          Gagandip Singh has been chasing the stage since he was eight years old.
        </p>
        <p>
          He came up on retro pop — {influences.retro.join(', ')} — the records built
          to move a room of strangers who had nothing else in common. That instinct
          never left. It just found better equipment.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first show was in {site.careerStart}, a modest club, back when the Indian
          DJ scene was still deciding whether it existed. {yearsActive} years later
          the count runs to {venueCount}-plus venues, six concurrent residencies, Goa
          New Year main stages, and a college circuit that reaches from IIT Delhi to
          SRCC to AIIMS.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-gold py-1 pl-5 text-body">
          <p class="italic">
            “I'm generally this calm and patient person who loves music and enjoys his
            time with family. But when I'm on stage, it's a whole different story. In
            that moment it's like I possess a hive mind — like I know what they want.
            I love the energy of being on stage. I can be whoever I want to be.”
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          The sound is {genres.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and {genres.at(-1)} — built for
          floors, not for playlists. And increasingly it is his own: inspired by
          {' '}{influences.production.join(' and ')}, he spends most of his time off the
          circuit in the studio, producing and remixing under {contact.label}.
        </p>
        <p>
          Forty-plus campus festivals is an unusual line on any DJ's résumé. It is also
          the most honest one. A college crowd is young, enormous, and completely
          replaced every three years — there is no coasting on a set that worked last
          season. Play forty of those and you stop guessing what a floor wants.
        </p>
        <p>
          Next: touring internationally, with the same records that have been working
          rooms across India for {yearsActive} years.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <BookingCTA />
</Base>
